From b372f67bceb98cd9f08a187a7e5a8439572a3bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lattice Bridge <bridge@lattice.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:13:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] lattice: authorized native supply change for the
 lattice-bridge builtin

Agave rejects any instruction or transaction whose lamport sum changes
(UnbalancedInstruction / UnbalancedTransaction). Native LAT issuance and
burn need exactly one, narrowly scoped exception:

- TransactionContext::record_native_supply_change(delta) lets the
  currently executing instruction declare that it created (delta > 0) or
  destroyed (delta < 0) lamports after crediting/debiting an account. It
  is only accepted when the current program is LATTICE_BRIDGE_PROGRAM_ID
  (Geuc2RbbzoWXSNYRyVDcjM5fZx6raKgf45y1bQr6aSzN) at top-level stack
  height; there is no syscall, so SBF programs cannot reach it.
- The per-instruction balance check therefore still holds for every other
  lamport movement; the SVM end-of-transaction check now requires
  post_sum == pre_sum + native_supply_delta exactly.
- The delta is carried in AccountsDeltas (Some only on success) and the
  bank applies it to capitalization in commit_transactions. Failed
  transactions roll back and change nothing. Capitalization keeps
  matching the account-balance sum, which snapshot load re-verifies.

Tests: transaction-context unit tests for balanced mint, unrecorded mint,
wrong amount, other program, and CPI depth.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
